@title STORY • AMARA: TOO SENSITIVE
@bg art_studio_day
You're Amara Johnson. Winger. Detroit. Everyone says you're "too sensitive." You cry at commercials, at sunsets, at goals. Yours and the other team's.
@show simone
Simone: You're painting again. What's this one?
Amara: It's Drew. From swim. Is that weird?
Simone: You painted him underwater. With fish. That's very weird. It's also beautiful.
> [Sweet] "Should I give it to him?" -> a1
> [Good] "I'm keeping it. He doesn't even know my name." -> a2
*a1
@add Courage 2
Simone: Only if I can watch.
@jump a_done
*a2
Simone: He knows your name, Amara. Tyler told Brooke and Brooke told Maya and Maya told everybody.
*a_done
@bg campus_pool_day
You find Drew at the pool. You're holding the painting. Your hands are shaking.
> [Bold] Give it to him. Say "I made this." -> b1
> [Sweet] Leave it on his bag with a note. -> b2
*b1
@add Courage 3
Drew: (staring at it) ...You made this? Of me?
Amara: Is it weird?
Drew: It's the nicest thing anyone's ever done for me. Can I hang it in my room? Can I... take you to dinner?
You cry. Of course you cry. He laughs, but in a nice way, and hands you his towel.
@jump end
*b2
@add Courage 1
That night he DMs you a picture of it on his wall. "who made this?? i need to thank them." You reply "me." Your phone rings in under a minute.
*end
Amara Johnson feels everything. This year, she finds out that's not too much. It's exactly enough.
